            "synthesis_para" : "The CeO2-Co3O4 mixed oxide catalysts with different Co/(Co+Ce) atomic ratios were prepared by citric acid sol-gel method as follows. Appropriate amounts of Co(NO3)2 . 6H2O, Ce(NO3)3 . 6H2O and citric acid (citric acid/((Co+Ce)=1.2, molar ratio) were dissolved in distilled water at room temperature and stirred for 15 min, then gradually heated to 80 ºC and kept at this temperature for 3 h with stirring, resulting in the formation of gel. Further, the resultant gel was dried at 100 ºC for 12 h, followed by calcination at 450 ºC for 4 h in air. The prepared catalysts are thus referred to as Ce1–xCox (x indicates the atomic ratio of Co/(Co+Ce)). For comparison, pure Co3O4 and CeO2 were also prepared following the same procedure.",
