            "synthesis_para" : "Citrate acid complex-combustion synthesis: Ce(NO3)3·6H2O, and Cu(NO3)2·3H2O are used as precursors, with the Cu/Ce molar ratio of 0.05:0.95 and 0:1, respectively [44]. Synthesis is controlled at 70 °C, citrate acid is dropped until pH reaches 1.0. Temperature increases to 100 °C, paste is formed and temperature arrives at 150 °C until the combustion is over and powder is formed, then it is ground, baked at 100 °C for 2 h, conveyed to a muffle and calcined at 550 °C for 5 h. The final catalysts are marked as Cu0.05Ce0.95-CA and CeO2-CA, respectively.",
